      "KEY WORDS: Risk Indicator — a measurable condition that signals increased probability of failure, incident, or non-compliance. Leading Indicator — a metric that changes before an event occurs (predictive). Lagging Indicator — a metric that records what already happened (reactive). Risk Matrix — a framework ranking risks by severity and likelihood. Failure Mode — the specific way in which equipment or a process can fail. Near-Miss — an event that could have resulted in injury, damage, or loss but did not.",
